        {
          "analysis": "This is an ARM-based DDoS bot. The malware fingerprints the compromised device by checking files like `/proc/version` and `/system/build.prop` to identify specific vendors (e.g., TP-Link, Zhone). It then daemonizes to run in the background and connects to a hardcoded C2 server at `209.141.49.229:6678`. Upon receiving commands such as `udp`, `std`, `icmp-hex`, or `fortnite`, it launches various DDoS flood attacks using functions like `udp_flood`, `std_attack`, and `fortnite_attack`.",
          "source": "palm",
